## Part 4 — Render service (FastAPI wrapping the LangGraph app)

**Endpoints:**
- `POST /run` — body: `{ run_id, citizen_id, query }`. Validates the `X-Sahayak-Internal-Secret` header against an env var (only the Edge Function knows this value — Render must reject everything else, including direct public requests). Loads the citizen's `profiles` row itself (service-role client), then kicks off the LangGraph invocation as a background task (`asyncio.create_task` or FastAPI's `BackgroundTasks`), and returns `202 Accepted` immediately.
- `POST /track` — (stretch, see 3.2) writes a tracker notification on submission.
- `GET /health` — trivial health check; use it to pre-warm Render before your demo slot (free/low tiers cold-start, and a 20-second cold start mid-pitch is a bad look — hit this endpoint a minute before you go on stage).

**Env vars on Render:** `GROQ_API_KEY`, `SUPABASE_URL`, `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` (never exposed to the browser — this service is the one place it's allowed to live outside the Supabase dashboard itself), `INTERNAL_SHARED_SECRET`.

**Python deps:** `langgraph`, `langchain`, `langchain-groq` (or raw `groq` SDK if you want less abstraction to debug under time pressure — for a hackathon, calling Groq's OpenAI-compatible endpoint directly with the `openai` SDK pointed at `https://api.groq.com/openai/v1` is a defensible simplification if LangGraph's LangChain-model wrapper gives you trouble), `supabase-py`, `fastapi`, `uvicorn`.

