## Part 7 — Task order

1. Apply the Part 0 fixes (1, 2, 6 at minimum — they're load-bearing for everything below).
2. Stand up the Render service with just `/health` deployed — confirm Render↔Supabase connectivity (a script that inserts a test `agent_events` row) before writing any LangGraph logic.
3. Build the LangGraph graph with all five nodes returning **hardcoded structured output** first (no Groq calls yet) — verify the graph shape, conditional routing, and Supabase writes end-to-end.
4. Swap each node's hardcoded output for a real Groq call, one node at a time, testing after each swap.
5. Build `orchestrate-agent-run` Edge Function, wire the internal secret.
6. Tighten `agent_events`/`audit_logs` RLS (drop client insert access).
7. Wire `/assistant` to the Edge Function + Realtime.
8. Wire `/admin/agents` to the same Realtime pattern.
9. Load-test with 3–4 concurrent runs to see real Groq rate-limit behavior before you're relying on it live.
10. Full rehearsal: reset demo state via the (now-complete) `seed-demo-data`, run the whole citizen journey twice back-to-back to confirm reproducibility.

## Part 8 — Acceptance checklist
- [ ] A real, un-cached query typed into `/assistant` produces a genuinely different scheme match than a different query (proves it's not secretly still keyword-matched)
- [ ] Killing the Render service mid-run leaves the UI in a sane "action required / retry" state, not an infinite spinner
- [ ] `/admin/agents` shows two different citizens' runs interleaved correctly when triggered close together
- [ ] A forced Groq `429` (temporarily drop your rate limit by hammering the API in another terminal) is visibly handled, not fatal
- [ ] `audit_logs` cannot be written to from the browser console using the citizen's own session (confirms the RLS tightening actually took)
- [ ] Cold-start Render, then immediately run the full demo flow, to know your worst-case pitch-day timing

## Part 9 — Explicit non-goals for Phase 2
- No real OCR/vision — Document Agent reasons over `document_requirements` rows, not file contents (Phase 3).
- No retry/resume of a half-finished run — if a run fails, the citizen re-triggers from `/assistant`; don't build checkpointing yet.
- No horizontal scaling concerns on Render — a single instance is fine for a hackathon's concurrent-judges load.

